      ":question/problem": "What is the sum of the leading entries of the $1\\text{st},$ $2\\text{nd},$ and $4\\text{th}$ rows in the matrix $A,$ given below?\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}4 & 2 & -2 & -5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -6 & 8 \\\\ 0 & -4 & 0 & 9 \\\\ -9 & -6 & -1 & 4\\end{bmatrix}\n$$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "The first non-zero entry of each row (from left to right) is the leading entry. \n\nTherefore, the leading entries of the $1\\text{st},$ $2\\text{nd},$ and $4\\text{th}$ rows of $A$ are $4,$ $-6,$ and $-9$, respectively.\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}4 & 2 & -2 & -5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -6 & 8 \\\\ 0 & -4 & 0 & 9 \\\\ -9 & -6 & -1 & 4\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nSo, the answer is $4+(-6)+(-9)=-11.$",
