      ":question/id": "85b4365b-b9a7-52b8-b078-b53744777200",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
      ":question/problem": "What is the sum of the leading entries of the $1\\text{st}$ and $2\\text{nd}$ rows in the matrix $A,$ given below?\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 0 & -1 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & -7 \\\\ 0 & -5 & -6 & -7 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 7\\end{bmatrix}\n$$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "The first non-zero entry of each row (from left to right) is the leading entry. \n\nTherefore, the leading entries of the $1\\text{st}$ and $2\\text{nd}$ rows of $A$ are $-1$ and $-7$, respectively.\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 0 & -1 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & -7 \\\\ 0 & -5 & -6 & -7 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 7\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nSo, the answer is $-1+(-7)=-8.$",
